linux.defconfig: the 32-bit kernel configuration (savedefconfig format),
applied before ../common/linux.fragment.

Made from the Raspberry Pi kernel's bcm2709_defconfig (Pi 2, 3, 3 B+) +
linux.fragment with "make localmodconfig": only the modules in
../common/kernel-modules.lsmod are kept (91 of 1281). That list is the
module set of the trimmed 64-bit kernel (see ../arm64/linux.defconfig.README):
what a CosmosEx loads (this image and a stock Raspbian unit), plus what's
needed on demand (cifs, nfsd, joydev, xpad, all HID device drivers, i2c-dev,
Wi-Fi, cdc_ether for QEMU).

To regenerate (e.g. after a kernel update), in the build container:
  cd /work/output-armv7/build/linux-custom
  export PATH=/work/output-armv7/host/bin:$PATH
  make ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-buildroot-linux-gnueabihf- \
       LSMOD=/src/board/cosmosex/common/kernel-modules.lsmod localmodconfig
  make ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-buildroot-linux-gnueabihf- savedefconfig
  cp defconfig /src/board/cosmosex/armv7/linux.defconfig
A module that's missing: add CONFIG_<X>=m to ../common/linux.fragment (and
its name to kernel-modules.lsmod).
